DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI SecretRotationPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure
@Observable state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing loading/empty/error/success
plus the 503 subsystem-unavailable variant over an injectable SecretRotationDataSource seam whose
value types mirror the rotation-tracker wire `Status` 1:1 (production binds
OperatorConfidenceStore.secretRotation() through the seam). The page reproduces the web chrome
(title/subtitle), the subsystem-unavailable AlertBanner, the overdue-rotations AlertBanner (gated on
critical>0 with the interpolated count), the four summary StatCards (Tracked / OK / Warn / Critical,
with ShieldCheck/AlertTriangle SF Symbols, shown only when items>0), and the rotation-status
GlassPanel with an adaptive table — a columnar Grid on macOS/iPad and per-secret cards on iPhone —
covering all six web columns (Kind+target, Last rotated+relative, Age, Expires+days-remaining,
Warn/critical thresholds, severity badge) using the P2 tokens + P3 shared components (no hand-rolled
glass). Every visible string resolves from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names (21 keys
added); display formatting (fmtNumber/formatDateTime/formatDate/formatRelative) is ported and
unit-tested. Verified on BOTH idioms by isolated Swift 6 strict-concurrency type-checks (0/0) and an
executed model harness (46/46). The full xcodebuild scheme is RED ONLY due to two pre-existing,
out-of-scope sibling errors (forbidden to commit-fix), with ZERO diagnostics in any of my files.

